00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:42.140
Before I examine with you the holiday of Hanukkah, let me tell you a little bit about the historical antecedents.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:55.240
At one time, up to the year 597 before the coming era, which means over 2600 years ago, or more or less about 2600 years ago, we were an independent people.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:05:01.240
There was the kingdom of Judea, of Yehuda. We are called Jews therefore.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:04.240
And we were independent. We were the head of king.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.240
The longest dynasty in recorded history was the dynasty of King David.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:21.240
His children remained in power from about the year 1000 before the coming era to the year 597.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:26.980
was no other dynasty in history that lasted so long. You know that? There wasn't. Even

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:31.720
the King of England or the Queen of England today, they have not lasted as long as the

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:40.840
King David dynasty. So we had our own king and we had our own government and so on. Now,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:49.740
for reasons that are not important for this lecture, the year 597, Jerusalem was conquered

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:54.160
by Babylonia.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:56.700
However, which is also important to know is

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:00.760
