were others who said no, the Rabbi is wrong, and we're going to follow what the Torah says.

01:06:45.320 --> 01:06:50.640
By the way, that's not my intention, don't misquote me and don't take me out of context.

01:06:50.640 --> 01:06:59.400
But this same argument was said by a very intelligent man, Eichmann.

01:06:59.400 --> 01:07:04.720
Eichmann claimed, I knew that killing the Jews was wrong.

01:07:04.720 --> 01:07:10.400
I loved the Jews, I respected the Jews, but I obeyed orders.

01:07:10.400 --> 01:07:15.380
My authority, my Fuhrer said, kill the Jews.

01:07:15.380 --> 01:07:18.320
And although I thought, I knew that it was wrong, I did it.

01:07:18.320 --> 01:07:19.320
That was the claim.

01:07:19.320 --> 01:07:20.640
I don't know whether he believed it or not.

01:07:20.640 --> 01:07:23.260
But that was his claim in the court of Israel.

01:07:24.480 --> 01:07:29.220
And the same thing, if you know, for instance, the Kohen is wrong,

01:07:30.660 --> 01:07:34.240
who was the priest of the time, or the Sanhedrin is wrong,

01:07:34.860 --> 01:07:37.580
and you listen because they are making, you are in the same situation,

01:07:37.740 --> 01:07:39.100
you are not different than this.

01:07:39.100 --> 01:07:42.140
You have to follow what the law says, what the Torah says.

01:07:42.220 --> 01:07:43.880
We have certain law, we have certain Torah,

01:07:44.460 --> 01:07:50.520
which transcends human office, an office or a title or a position.

01:07:50.640 --> 01:07:52.240
It is what the Torah says.

01:07:52.960 --> 01:07:55.500
Ultimately, is it haram or is it not haram?

01:07:56.200 --> 01:07:57.520
What does Yishuha Harukh say?

01:07:58.080 --> 01:08:01.340
Does Yishuha Harukh say it's forbidden or says it's permitted?

01:08:02.500 --> 01:08:08.060
And this is something that nobody could, this is a decision that only you could make and you must make.

01:08:08.740 --> 01:08:10.160
This is the whole meaning of Hanukkah.

01:08:10.620 --> 01:08:13.480
It's a very important, it's a very profound struggle.

01:08:13.480 --> 01:08:21.640
And we say in the tefillah, it's not only about a fight with goyim, but also,

01:08:22.360 --> 01:08:25.500
Yes?

01:08:26.040 --> 01:08:29.960
There were the saddiqim who were defeated by the saddiqim.

01:08:30.720 --> 01:08:30.880
Yes?

01:08:33.680 --> 01:08:36.600
It was a question of a fight of brother against brother.

01:08:37.620 --> 01:08:38.940
It was a fight on ideology.

01:08:38.940 --> 01:08:41.920
It's a very interesting thing, this of Hanukkah.

01:08:41.920 --> 01:08:43.920
Elliot, you raised your hand before.

01:08:43.920 --> 01:08:46.920
You mentioned that Shukran al-Rukh, they didn't have that.

01:08:46.920 --> 01:08:53.920
No, no, but it's of course as an example. I mean, I try to speak enough, but they had the tradition, the Tarash of Al-Payy.

01:08:53.920 --> 01:08:58.920
So what would they say, what was right and what was wrong? How can you say that the Quran al-Ghazal was wrong?

01:08:58.920 --> 01:09:08.920
That's the point. But they had the traditions, the Tarash of Al-Payy, that they're being for the parents, the grandparents.

01:09:08.920 --> 01:09:12.580
They say, it is haram to eat pig.

01:09:13.240 --> 01:09:19.380
And the Kohen Gadol says, no, but if you sacrifice this pig, yes, for an idol,

01:09:19.900 --> 01:09:23.020
and this idol is for God, then it's permitted.

01:09:23.680 --> 01:09:25.160
And you say, Hashem, I say, this is not.

01:09:26.080 --> 01:09:27.740
Now the question is, whom you want to follow?

01:09:29.280 --> 01:09:31.840
In these problems, you know, the problem is a very interesting problem.

01:09:32.000 --> 01:09:32.660
It's very interesting.

01:09:33.020 --> 01:09:34.120
The problem is very complex.

01:09:34.260 --> 01:09:37.540
I'm not saying it's an easy problem to solve.

01:09:37.540 --> 01:09:41.780
I'm just telling you what the Jews had confronted at the time.

01:09:42.560 --> 01:09:47.560
It's a question of almost individual conscience versus established authority.

01:09:49.520 --> 01:09:52.760
And there were many people who searched in the conscience,

01:09:53.300 --> 01:09:57.400
and they say the Kohen Gadol is wrong, and the Sanhedrin is wrong.

01:09:58.860 --> 01:09:59.880
I'm going to fight it.

01:10:00.200 --> 01:10:01.940
And they fought it until they won.

01:10:02.460 --> 01:10:07.040
It's an interesting thing, because this is what makes this holiday,

01:10:07.540 --> 01:10:09.540
